{"id":52272,"ord":60,"n_segments":181,"prev":52271,"next":52273,"doc":{"id":"67256","title":"67256_Paul L. Howard oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Paul L. Howard","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/67256/","url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=67256"},"chapter":"Reel 2: Los Angeles musicians, the Apex and Cotton Club","title":"Sue Hoye in the 1934 Cotton Club review","category":"venue_city_scene","summary":"Willard shows a clipping about the Sebastian Cotton Club review with Sue Hoye and Patsy Hunter; Howard tires.","period":"1934","year_from":1934,"year_to":1934,"words":166,"start":[99,9],"end":[100,18],"url":"https://semlab.io/linked-jazz-transcripts/?t=67256#s52272","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[{"name":"Cotton Club","focus":1,"city":"Culver City"}],"bands":[{"name":"Les Hite Orchestra","focus":0,"leader":"Les Hite"}]},"people":[{"name":"Susie Howard","qid":null,"n":3},{"name":"Paul L. Howard","qid":"Q7151403","n":2},{"name":"Lionel Hampton","qid":"Q313525","n":1},{"name":"Les Hite","qid":"Q1820533","n":1},{"name":"Frank Sebastian","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Patsy Hunter","qid":null,"n":1},{"name":"Eddie Anderson","qid":"Q1751027","n":1}],"story":{"theme":32,"theme_name":"Going west: California and the Los Angeles scene","community":57,"community_name":"Going west: moving to and working in California","core":true},"blocks":[{"p":99,"b":9,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"No. Now, Susie worked out there at the -- what's the name of that place?"},{"p":99,"b":10,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Susie worked there?"},{"p":99,"b":11,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"She worked out at the -- the place out of -- I can't think of the name of it."},{"p":99,"b":12,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Cotton Club?"},{"p":99,"b":13,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Yeah, Cotton Club."},{"p":100,"b":0,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"(Inaudible.)"},{"p":100,"b":1,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"1934, it says, right here."},{"p":100,"b":2,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"I don't even see it."},{"p":100,"b":3,"s":"MS. WILLARD","x":"It says, 'Colored Review is Hit At Sebastian,' and it mentions Sue Hoye there, and Ebony Steppers. It mentions Patsy Hunter, too. Eddie Anderson."},{"p":100,"b":4,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"See it, Paul?"},{"p":100,"b":5,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Let's see, Les Hite and Frank Sebastian, Lionel Hampton, don't give you all the names of the men playing in this --"},{"p":100,"b":6,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"No, probably not all of them."},{"p":100,"b":7,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"No."},{"p":100,"b":8,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Just some of the more famous names."},{"p":100,"b":9,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"(Unintelligible.)— get out of here."},{"p":100,"b":10,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Who will?"},{"p":100,"b":11,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"That's all right."},{"p":100,"b":12,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Huh?"},{"p":100,"b":13,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"That's okay."},{"p":100,"b":14,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"You mean, you're in trouble?"},{"p":100,"b":15,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Yeah."},{"p":100,"b":16,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"No, you'll be all right, Paul. You don't think so? So, are you getting tired today?"},{"p":100,"b":17,"s":"MR. HOWARD","x":"Yep, I'm tired now."},{"p":100,"b":18,"s":"MR. COLLETTE","x":"Okay. Anything else you want to say to him before --"}]}